# Local first — live only on request

Before pushing to git and updating the live website, show the changes locally first and create (or reuse) a local server.

Whenever the user asks for any update, check it locally first. Once it is finalized, and they tell you to update the live website, then only commit and push (`website/` → `origin main`).

- Serve `website/` (default `http://127.0.0.1:5500`).
- Do not `git commit` or `git push` in `website/` unless they clearly ask to update live / deploy / push.
- Live site: https://abhishekbhowmick.netlify.app/ from GitHub `azaad0208/portfolio`.
